    "sourceDescription": "To support the implementation of the Wholesale Credit strategy across South and East Africa through effective partnership with in-country Credit Heads and credit teams. The role provides specialist credit expertise, consolidated regional portfolio insight and independent challenge to support prudent credit decision-making, compliance with approved facilities and the timely identification and escalation of emerging risks. The role operates through partnership, expertise and influence. It does not replace the authority, delegated mandates or accountability of in-country Credit Heads, who remain accountable for local credit decisions, portfolio management and regulatory compliance. Regional Credit Partnership and Oversight Partner with in-country Credit Heads and credit teams to support effective credit-risk management across South and East Africa. Provide specialist advice and constructive challenge on material, complex or higher-risk credit matters. Promote the consistent application of credit standards, while recognising local regulation, market conditions and delegated mandates. Support countries in monitoring compliance with approved facilities, credit conditions and applicable policies. Identify and escalate material regional, systemic and cross-border credit risks. Facilitate the sharing of credit insight and sound practice across the region. Sovereign and Jurisdictional Risk Assess sovereign, macroeconomic, political, regulatory and jurisdictional risks across South and East Africa. Translate country developments into clear credit, portfolio and capital implications. Support in-country teams in assessing the effect of jurisdictional risk on existing exposures, proposed transactions and growth plans. Provide specialist insight to inform risk appetite, country limits and portfolio strategy. Support credit assessments relating to entry into, or expansion within, African markets. Credit and Transaction Support Partner with in-country Credit Heads, credit teams and transactors on material or complex transactions. Provide specialist advice and constructive challenge on credit proposals requiring regional, sovereign or jurisdictional expertise. Assess the wider country, regional, portfolio and capital implications of proposed transactions. Provide evidence-based recommendations to credit and portfolio committees. Support countries in balancing commercial opportunities with prudent risk management and approved risk appetite. Portfolio Reporting and Credit Analytics Own the consolidated regional portfolio view across South and East Africa, drawing on information and analysis provided by in-country teams. Lead regional reporting on portfolio performance, concentrations, limits, early-warning indicators, watchlist exposures and non-performing exposures. Partner with in-country Credit Heads to interpret material changes in portfolio quality and determine appropriate management actions. Provide specialist expertise and challenge on IFRS 9 impairment and expected credit loss, including staging, key assumptions, forward-looking scenarios and management overlays. Assess the implications of regulatory and economic capital for portfolio strategy and sustainable growth. Coordinate regional stress testing and scenario analysis covering sovereign, macroeconomic, sector and jurisdictional risks. Present material portfolio developments, emerging risks and recommended actions to relevant governance forums. Credit Models, Workflow and Infrastructure Provide specialist input into credit-model performance and governance, including model limitations, validation findings and remediation priorities. Assess the implications of model performance for credit decisions, impairment, portfolio reporting and capital. Partner with country teams and specialist functions to identify and address weaknesses in credit data, workflows, systems and infrastructure. Support the consistent and appropriate use of credit models and reporting standards across the region. Escalate material data-quality, model, infrastructure or control concerns through the appropriate governance forums. Governance and Stakeholder Coordination Coordinate regional credit governance and maintain an appropriate framework for oversight, reporting and escalation. Support countries in applying approved credit policies, mandates and control standards. Maintain clear records of material decisions, agreed actions, accountable owners and delivery dates. Engage with Credit, Risk, Finance, Internal Audit and relevant regulatory stakeholders. Monitor agreed actions and escalate material delays, dependencies or control weaknesses. Provide visibility of regional priorities, strategic initiatives, delivery risks, team capacity and vacancies. Promote the sharing of portfolio insight, lessons learned and effective credit practices across the region. People Leadership Lead an inclusive, accountable and performance-led team. Set clear performance objectives and provide regular, evidence-based feedback. Develop technical credit capability, commercial judgement and leadership capacity. Delegate authority appropriately while maintaining clear accountability. Maintain appropriate succession plans and a sustainable regional credit talent pipeline. Promote sound judgement, ethical conduct and consistently high standards of execution. Accountability The role owns: The consolidated regional portfolio view and associated reporting. Regional coordination and escalation of material credit and country-risk matters. The quality of specialist advice and constructive challenge provided to countries. The regional governance and reporting framework. Performance management and development of direct reports. The role oversees and supports: In-country teams on complex credit origination, portfolio, ORM and emerging-risk matters. Regional consistency in credit reporting, governance and standards. Regional interpretation of IFRS 9 impairment, capital, risk-appetite and stress-testing outcomes. Regional themes relating to credit models, data, workflows and infrastructure. Recruiting and retaining talent Skills Required Regulatory and economic capital Credit-risk data, analytics and portfolio reporting Credit models and model governance Risk appetite, concentration management and stress testing Credit workflow, systems and infrastructure Wholesale credit assessment and portfolio management Sovereign, country and jurisdictional risk assessment Pan-African governance and stakeholder coordination Executive communication and constructive challenge Minimum Qualifications Both requirements are mandatory: Honours degree in Accounting/Finance or Economics; or Chartered Accountant South Africa, CA(SA); or MBA; or CFA; or Mcom ( Finance or Economics) Experience Required Significant senior leadership experience in wholesale, corporate or investment-banking credit. Experience operating across multiple African markets, including South and East Africa. Strong experience in credit assessment, transaction structuring, portfolio management and complex credit matters. Experience in portfolio reporting. Strong understanding of regulatory and economic capital, risk appetite and stress testing. Experience in credit models, model governance and credit infrastructure. Experience assessing sovereign, macroeconomic and jurisdictional risk. Proven participation in senior credit, portfolio, impairment and risk-governance forums. Strong people leadership and cross-border stakeholder-management experience. Behavioural Capabilities Independent credit judgement Strategic and commercial thinking Partnership and collaboration Constructive, evidence-based challenge Executive-level influence Governance and control discipline Decisive and accountable leadership Ethical judgement and professional integrity",
